<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaHuttCartel.xml                          Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  FACTION_SPEC.md section 2. Faction 2 of 14.

  ParentName is `OutlanderFactionBase` (R24), which supplies factionNameMaker,
  settlementNameMaker, factionIconPath, techLevel Industrial, leaderTitle,
  allowedArrivalTemperatureRange and a full set of pawnGroupMakers. Everything
  restated below is either a value the parent does not give at all, or one the
  dossier contradicts.

  🔴 `colorSpectrum` IS NOT INHERITED. Measured on the shipped abstracts:
  `OutlanderFactionBase` and `TribeBase` supply NO colorSpectrum — only
  `PirateBandBase` does. R24's table says otherwise and is wrong on that one
  field. A faction without it is set on 76 of 87 live defs, so the world map
  draws it broken. It is set explicitly here and in all six siblings.

  ✅ THE IDEO BLOCK IS IN THIS FILE. R23 said to omit it and add it in one pass
  when the text existed; the text exists (`faction_religions_spec.md`) and that
  pass landed here rather than in a separate file. 🔴 It has to be here before
  the worldgen click: an ideo is generated once, at world creation, and a
  `fixedIdeo` added afterwards does not retrofit an existing world.

  🔴 `Jawa_Spawn_Hutt` APPEARS IN Settlement AND Trader guards ONLY, NEVER in a
  Combat group. A Hutt does not go on raids; it is met at home or on a caravan.

  Pawn kinds verified present in the 2026-08-14 dump (585 mods) and mapped to
  their owning mod for `MayRequire`:
      RimMandrake_Nikto · RimMandrake_NiktoTribal          mandrake.starwarsraces
      Bantha · Dewback                        Mlie.StarWarsAnimalCollection
      Jawa_Gamorrean_* · Jawa_Spawn_Hutt      OURS, this same mod - no MayRequire
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Jawa_HuttCartel</defName>
    <label>Hutt Cartel</label>
    <fixedName>Hutt Cartel</fixedName>
    <description>Wealthy, decentralised and entirely transactional. The Cartel owns the oases and sells water at whatever the buyer can be made to pay, and it holds the only non-Imperial orbital node on the planet — the door off-world, and the reason everyone keeps taking its calls.\n\nIt is hostile the way a creditor is hostile. Nothing about it is personal, and everything about it is negotiable.</description>
    <pawnSingular>Cartel enforcer</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>Cartel enforcers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>Lord</leaderTitle>
    <!-- 🔴 WITHOUT THIS THE FACTION IS NOT ON THE CONFIGURE FACTIONS SCREEN, and a world
         built through that screen may not contain it at all. Measured 2026-08-22
         (AUTHORED_FACTIONS_OFF_THE_SCREEN_1): seven of our eight read -1 here.
         `FactionGenerator.ConfigurableFactions` is
             from f in DefDatabase<FactionDef>.AllDefs
             where f.maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation > 0
             orderby f.configurationListOrderPriority
         and vanilla writes 9999 on the CONCRETE defs (OutlanderCivil, TribeCivil,
         Pirate), never on the abstract bases we inherit - so ours defaulted to -1.
         ⚠️ `requiredCountAtGameStart` is NOT a safety net for this.
         `FactionGenerator.InitializeFactions` reads it ONLY when `factions == null`;
         worldgen through the screen passes the configured list and adds it verbatim.
         A dev quicktest takes the null path, which is why these factions generated
         when CHECK measured them and why that measurement does not transfer.
         ⛔ Set on OUR def, never on the abstract base - patching OutlanderFactionBase
         would hand a screen row to every outlander faction in 578 mods.
         🔑 The priority sorts ASCENDING, so the negative numbers put the campaign's own
         eight factions at the TOP of the page the owner builds the one world from.
         Vanilla's own rows are 10-60. -->
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>-98</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <categoryTag>Outlander</categoryTag>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>1</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <humanlikeFaction>true</humanlikeFaction>
    <canMakeRandomly>true</canMakeRandomly>
    <maxCountAtGameStart>1</maxCountAtGameStart>
    <!-- 8 settlements, all oasis tiles. -->
    <settlementGenerationWeight>1.15</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <!-- Hostile but negotiable: neither flag is set true. -->
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <canRequestTraders>true</canRequestTraders>

    <factionNameMaker>NamerFactionOutlander</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>NamerSettlementOutlander</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/HuttCartel</factionIconPath>
    <!-- R22: sickly gold. -->
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.72,0.62,0.25)</li>
      <li>(0.58,0.48,0.18)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>

    <!--
      ================================================================
      THE RECKONING OF DEBTS — faction_religions_spec.md entry 2 (B54)
      ================================================================
      `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim from the spec; they are the only
      strings the engine renders. ⭐ CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED: they had drifted apart —
      this file and the spec each carried a different, complete paragraph. Reconciled
      2026-08-19 by BLENDING them, on the owner's ruling that both were exceptional and
      entirely in synchrony. The spec now carries the identical 665-character string.

      ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET — it suppresses the description entirely.

      `requiredPreceptsOnly` is deliberately FALSE here, unlike the Empire's.
      The doctrine is not the whole point for the Cartel, so the generator is
      left room to add colour and the faction reads as a people rather than a
      clause.

      `VME_Structure_Corporate` has deityCount 1-1, so EXACTLY ONE deityPreset.
      Structure meme goes FIRST in `forcedMemes`.

      `disallowedPrecepts` blacklists the other six Execution precepts so the
      issue's default cannot win — no meme in this set carries an Execution
      group, so without the blacklist the faction would land on
      `Execution_HorribleIfInnocent`, the exact opposite of the doctrine.
      ⚠️ Whether the generator then takes the weight-0 survivor or leaves the
      issue empty is UNVERIFIED offline; it needs a live read.
    -->
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <requiredPreceptsOnly>false</requiredPreceptsOnly>
    <ideoName>the Reckoning of Debts</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>Everything on this world evaporates, freezes, or is stolen. A debt does none of these. It is the only object that survives crossing between the faces, and so it is the only true account of a person: what you owe is what you are. The water you drank this morning, the air in the dome, the years your mother did not work — all of it is on the ledger. We do not forgive, because forgiving destroys value that belonged to everyone, and because forgiveness is a rounding error and we do not round. We sell the smoke and we breathe the smoke. Pay, and you are family. Do not pay, and you are inventory. What the book cannot settle, the pit does. There is no third column.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Structure_Corporate</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Trader</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Guilty</li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_Gladiator</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">HighLife</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Corporate</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Hedonist</li>
    </styles>
    <deityPresets>
      <li>
        <nameType><name>the Ledger</name><type>That Which Does Not Forgive</type></nameType>
        <gender>None</gender>
        <iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath> <!-- vanilla; Anomaly's HoraxCult uses this exact path. validate_patch.py warns on it because the texture is inside a Unity bundle, not a loose file. -->
      </li>
    </deityPresets>
    <disallowedPrecepts>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_Abhorrent</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_Horrible</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_HorribleIfInnocent</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_DontCare</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_RespectedIfGuilty</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Execution_Classic</li>
    </disallowedPrecepts>

    <!-- R27: `xenotypeSet` is the SECOND inherit trap. `OutlanderFactionBase`
         ships five vanilla xenotypes (Hussar · Dirtmole · Genie · Neanderthal ·
         Starjack) and `PirateBandBase` ships nine; a child set is APPENDED to
         them, so without this opt-out the faction fields Hussars in a Star Wars
         campaign. The species below are this repo's own, copied out of the
         three colliding packs so none of them has to stay installed.
         ⚠️ The CHANCES are BUILD's, not the spec's — R27 gives species, not
         numbers. They sum to ~1.00, with the dossier
         lead species heaviest.
         ⚠️ Baseliner is one of the entries and it is NOT zero, so plain humans DO
         generate at that rate. The comment used to claim otherwise. Retune freely;
         nothing depends on them. -->
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <RimMandrakeHutt MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.145</RimMandrakeHutt>
        <RimMandrakeKlatoonian MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.145</RimMandrakeKlatoonian>
        <RimMandrakeNikto MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.145</RimMandrakeNikto>
        <RimMandrakeAqualish MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeAqualish>
        <RimMandrakeDevaronian MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeDevaronian>
        <RimMandrakeFalleen MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeFalleen>
        <RimMandrakeGamorrean MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeGamorrean>
        <RimMandrakePyke MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakePyke>
        <RimMandrakeRodian MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeRodian>
        <RimMandrakeTrandoshan MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeTrandoshan>
        <RimMandrakeTwilek MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeTwilek>
        <RimMandrakeZeltron MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.048</RimMandrakeZeltron>
        <Baseliner>0.014</Baseliner>
        <RimMandrakeBothan MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeBothan>
        <RimMandrakeFeeorin MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeFeeorin>
        <MandrakeJawa MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</MandrakeJawa>
        <RimMandrakeKubaz MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeKubaz>
        <RimMandrakeMuun MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeMuun>
        <RimMandrakeOrtolan MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeOrtolan>
        <RimMandrakeUgnaught MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeUgnaught>
        <RimMandrakeZygerrian MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">0.014</RimMandrakeZygerrian>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>

    <!-- Inherit="False" IS LOAD-BEARING. RimWorld resolves inheritance AFTER
         patches, and a child `li` list is APPENDED to the parent's, not
         substituted for it. `OutlanderFactionBase` carries 8 group makers; without
         this opt-out the faction fields those too and raids arrive as
         vanilla pawns wearing our name. Vanilla itself writes it 314 times,
         9 of them on pawnGroupMakers. -->
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Grunt>10</Jawa_Hutt_Grunt>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Heavy>4</Jawa_Hutt_Heavy>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Specialist>2</Jawa_Hutt_Specialist>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Leader>1</Jawa_Hutt_Leader>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
        <traders>
          <RimMandrake_Nikto MayRequire="mandrake.starwarsraces">1</RimMandrake_Nikto>
        </traders>
        <guards>
          <Jawa_Gamorrean_Guard>6</Jawa_Gamorrean_Guard>
          <Jawa_Gamorrean_Enforcer>2</Jawa_Gamorrean_Enforcer>
          <Jawa_Spawn_Hutt>1</Jawa_Spawn_Hutt>
        </guards>
        <carriers>
          <Bantha MayRequire="Mlie.StarWarsAnimalCollection">6</Bantha>
          <Dewback MayRequire="Mlie.StarWarsAnimalCollection">5</Dewback>
        </carriers>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Grunt>10</Jawa_Hutt_Grunt>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Heavy>3</Jawa_Hutt_Heavy>
          <Jawa_Hutt_Specialist>2</Jawa_Hutt_Specialist>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
  </FactionDef>

</Defs>
